# KFB: a self-contained segment wrapper for `qop`, and its index semantics

`qopW Ms B1 G off` pushes the counts, parks the first `off` Gaussian entries of stack `0`,
runs `qop Ms` on the following `G · 2B1|Ms|` entries, and moves the parked prefix back:
on a clean managed state it replaces `pre ++ seg ++ rest` by `pre ++ qopL Ms B1 G seg ++ rest`.

Index semantics (`getD_qopL_diag`): with one diagonal matrix `diag(α, β)`, entry `j` of the
segment is multiplied by `α` or `β` according to bit `j / B1 mod 2`.
-/

